# Build context exclusions.
#
# Neither Backend/ nor Frontend/ had a .dockerignore, while both Dockerfiles end
# with `COPY . .`. That meant a local `docker build` copied .env (SAP passwords,
# LLM keys, the admin password), the SQLite database with every tenant's
# encrypted credentials, the auto-generated Fernet key, the SSH-tunnel helper and
# the whole test folder into the image layer - and image layers are readable by
# anyone who can pull the image.

# Secrets / credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
.fernet_key
data/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/
htmlcov/
.coverage

# Local tooling / notes
*.log
*.bak
*.zip
*.rar
start_ssh_tunnel.bat
doctor.py

# Tests are not needed in the runtime image (they need no ERP but they do
# double the image and ship fixtures).
tests/

# VCS
.git/
.gitignore
